[Ollie Connolly details](https://www.readoptional.com/p/the-art-of-play-sequencing-and-how) some of what makes the Payton offense tick. Philosophically one of the big divergences is where all the details show up. The Shanahan/McVay systems tend to employ very similar rules and are not neccessarily overly complicated. The bevy of details that lead to explosive plays tend to show up in what they are doing in other parts of the play. Whereas Payton is less wedded to particular personnel groupings and spends lots of time on protection plans. Part of this is because he wants to buy time for the routes to develop so his QB can hit them at the top of the drop.

We can also likely explain some of the discrepencies between in explosive play rate just due to overall team strength. If we examine the HSGP for Andy Reid we see that the explosiveness of the Chief's offense is fairly stable throughout his tenure. However, around the 2023 season a lot of analysts and pundits started to ask where did the explosive play element of the offense go? By this time offensive roster was significantly older, the line became a problem, and critically the Chiefs kept missing on pass catchers. 



::: {.cell}

